      "description": "Islam is projected to be the world's largest religion by 2035, surpassing Christianity, according to a new study released by the Pew Research Centre on Wednesday. Pew said if current trends continue, there will be more than 3.6 billion Muslims and just under three billion Christians worldwide by 2070.\nThe absolute number of Hindus in India and worldwide will rise from 1.2 billion in 2020 to 1.4 billion by 2070.\nBut the rest of the world's population -- i.e., all non-Hindus -- will grow at an even faster rate. As a result, Hindus will shrink slightly as a share of the global population, falling from 15 per cent in 2020 to 14 per cent in 2070.\nThe world's total population is projected to increase by 29 per cent between 2020 and 2070, with Christians growing by 30 per cent and Muslims by 80 per cent.\n\"The largest source of new members of major religions is not adults who convert to the faith, but babies who are born into the group,\" the Pew projections found.\nDuring 2020-2025, the ..",
